'''Lumina''' is a [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cat]] that can be obtained at an extremely low chance when playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES]] event. It was added in [[Version 8.5 Update|Version 8.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 478
|rarity = LR
|name1 = Lumina
|name2 = Luminalia
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Luminalia''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Lumina can be a generalist mid-ranger or a spammable anti-Alien meatshield for when there is a high chance of taking massive damage from a non-Alien enemy, which would make Lumina's Evolved Form more risky to bring. Besides that, there is little reason to pick this form above Luminalia, especially if you also own [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]], thus its DPS in general isn't exactly the best after all, as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] outshine it due to their spammability.

Despite being a fairly outclassed generalist, Lumina proves to be more useful than [[Ancient Egg: N102 (Rare Cat)|Catarzan]], as its fortified health against Aliens will help it survives longer than a stack of Catarzans, which will die quickly due to their mediocre health.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Luminalia is a niche but incredibly effective anti-alien unit. With a great deal of health and fast movement speed, it rushes to the front lines, and as long as there isn't much threat from non-aliens, it won't budge. The combination of good stats, [[Insanely Tough]] and 100% [[Weaken]] with full uptime means it has an absurd effective HP against aliens of 1,904,000 at level 30 (including its Weaken effect). Nearly 2 million effective HP at such low cost and recovery time means it is by far the best defensive anti-Alien unit in the game. And on top of this, it has solid DPS with its regular attacks. It can be used as a very useful support unit against decently short-ranged Aliens, whether it be in [[Into the Future]], [[Cats of the Cosmos]] or even [[Legend Stages]]. It is also a perfect counter to Starred Aliens, as it is immune to their Warp and can [[Barrier Breaker|break their Barriers]], making Aliens like [[Corporal Weyland]] and [[Project A]] that much easier. Its movement speed and high attack speed actually separate it from other [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Elemental Pixies]] to make it one of the most reliable Barrier Breakers available as well.

When using it in stages with significant non-Alien presence, Luminalia should be used as more of a generic midranger with supporting qualities. It can reach the frontline very quickly and Weaken the respective Alien threats such as [[Star Peng]], [[Commander Ostromeda]], and even [[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] for as long it can be kept alive. It has an unusually high base HP that keeps it healthy for a good amount of time even against non-targets, and its range is also fairly decent. Even in stages with no Alien, Luminalia is a perfectly capable midrange attacker with a high speed that can compliment aggressive play, with strong matchups against [[R.Ost]] and most of his variants.

Luminalia trivializes most Aliens-only stages, and is a perfectly competent midranger anywhere else, providing good utility in stages with even a single problematic Alien. However, in stages with non-targets, you must ensure it isn't hit by them excessively, making its role as a tank a fair bit dubious there. If a tank is truly needed for such stages, [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] will be much more capable so long as [[Warp]] is not present, though nothing is stopping you from using both in one lineup.

